Z||000000||ssalyers||10-07-2001||08:04 AM||||This has been happening for a while now, but I've decided to keep the car so I'd like to fix it.  When I turn the A/C to OFF (or anything other than A/C or VENT) I get a noise from the passenger side (under the dash) that sounds like a gear stripping and it does not stop (or I haven't let it go long enough).<P><BR>Thanks for any help,<P>Shawn||||reg||6
Z||000001||maryjane||10-07-2001||11:06 AM||||probably one of the air flow door motors has  disconnected or stripped out. They are electric, not vacum controlled as on other cars. Some are a pain to get to. You will have to feel around in the general area to find which one. Never been into mine much so I don't know exactly what to look for. Good luck. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-07-2001||02:23 PM||||There are notes about these controls in my cave.<P>it sounds like the mode motor has quit. That motor is behind the radio. (The other motor only runs when the MAX button is involved. The second motor opens the recirculation door.)<P>It only happens when one specific button changes? If so it could be a control problem or a bad contact in the motor.<P><BR>Do keep in mind.... certain mode changes do run the motor longer than others... In all cases the motor chould only run about 15-20 seconds max.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ssalyers||10-07-2001||08:14 PM||||Well, it definatly sounds stripped.....  I guess I'll get to it soon.  I'm in Florida and the A/C doesn't go off too much.  But the weather is gonna start getting nice soon, and I like the windows!!!<P><BR>--Shawn||||reg||12
